      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "WOW! Great cards! I drew:\n\
- **Draconic Roar** ({1}{R} - 3 damage to creature, or 3 damage to controller if I revealed a Dragon)\n\
- **Gonti, Lord of Luxury** ({2}{B}{B} - 2/3 with deathtouch, look at opponent's top 4 cards and exile one)\n\
- **Thieves' Guild Enforcer** ({B} - 1/1 flash, mills 2 when enters, grows with opponent graveyard)\n\
\n\
Also, opponent took damage! They're down to **8 HP** from 11 (must have been the upkeep damage from Stab Wound on Ravenous Giant: -2 life). And they played **Cultivate** (a ramp spell), which is now in their graveyard.\n\
\n\
Current board:\n\
- My life: 11 (took 4 damage from Ravenous Giant's upkeep ability at the start of their turn)\n\
- Opponent: 8 HP (critical!)\n\
\n\
My hand is STACKED with good cards. I need to evaluate the best play:\n\
\n\
**Option 1: Cast Draconic Roar** ({1}{R}) - Kill the Ravenous Giant or burn the player\n\
- If I reveal Hellkite Punisher as a Dragon, this does 3 damage to the Giant OR 3 damage to the opponent\n\
- This is likely lethal or close to it!\n\
\n\
**Option 2: Cast Thieves' Guild Enforcer** ({B}) - Flash creature, mills opponent\n\
- Cheap, and mills 2 of opponent's cards\n\
- Not as immediately threatening\n\
\n\
**Option 3: Cast Gonti** ({2}{B}{B}) - Exile one of opponent's top 4 cards\n\
- Expensive but powerful effect\n\
- Could steal something good\n\
\n\
**ANALYSIS:** I have **Draconic Roar** which can deal 3 damage directly if I reveal a Dragon (Hellkite Punisher). With opponent at 8 HP, if I cast Draconic Roar revealing Hellkite, that's 3 damage. Then I can cast Hellkite Punisher the next turn or later to finish. BUT WAIT—the Ravenous Giant can still block my creatures.\n\
\n\
Actually, let me re-read Draconic Roar: it deals 3 damage to the creature, and if I revealed a Dragon, it also deals 3 damage to the controller. So:\n\
- **Draconic Roar** targeting Ravenous Giant (revealing Hellkite Punisher) = 3 damage to Giant + 3 damage to opponent = 6 total damage to opponent = wins the game (8 → 2 HP)\n\
\n\
Wait, that's not quite right. Let me re-read: \"Deal 3 damage to target creature. If you revealed a Dragon card... deal 3 damage to that creature's controller.\"\n\
\n\
So it deals 3 to the creature AND 3 to the controller. That's 6 to the opponent if the Giant is the target. But the opponent has 8 HP, so 8 - 6 = 2 HP remaining. Not lethal yet, but close!\n\
\n\
**OPTIMAL PLAY:**\n\
1. Cast **Draconic Roar** revealing Hellkite Punisher, target Ravenous Giant → 3 damage to Giant, 3 damage to opponent (8 → 5 HP)\n\
2. Giant survives (4/3 - 3 = 1/3)\n\
3. Then I can cast Hellkite Punisher next turn and attack with Nocturnal Feeder again\n\
\n\
Actually wait, I need to carefully count: Ravenous Giant is 4/3. Draconic Roar does 3 damage. 4 - 3 = 1/3. So the Giant survives with 1/3.\n\
\n\
Hmm, but opponent will be at 5 HP. Then they can attack me. And I'm at 11 HP. Let me think about the bigger game plan.\n\
\n\
**Alternative:** Cast **Thieves' Guild Enforcer** first (cheap, mills opponent), then use my mana more efficiently. But that's slower.\n\
\n\
